From: fxtec-pro1x-guix
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6115-pro1x: keyboard backlight on at boot

Light the keyboard from the LED's probe, so the full-disk encryption
passphrase can be typed in the dark (author, 2026-11-07).  The
pro1x-kbd-backlight service sets it on its first pass once the system
is up (on while slid out with the panel on, off after a minute without
a key).

Ours (fxtec-pro1x-guix, 2026-11-07), on moWerk's 0007-pro1x-leds.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
@@ -201,7 +201,7 @@
 			function = LED_FUNCTION_KBD_BACKLIGHT;
 			color = <LED_COLOR_ID_WHITE>;
 			gpios = <&tlmm 103 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
-			default-state = "off";
+			default-state = "on";
 			pinctrl-names = "default";
 			pinctrl-0 = <&kbd_backlight_default>;
 		};
